[see bashrc]
##################################################
export ZCI_USER_CONFIGDIR=~/.config/zypp-team
export ZCI_UTILS_CHECKOUT=~/zypp-ci-utils
export ZCI_WORKSPACE=~/ZCI_WORKSPACE
if [ -d "$ZCI_UTILS_CHECKOUT" ]; then
    PATH="$ZCI_UTILS_CHECKOUT/zypp-team/bin:$PATH"
fi
[ -z "$SSH_AUTH_SOCK" -a -f . ~/.ssh4cron ] && . ~/.ssh4cron
##################################################

Setup:

- Copy the zypp-team-submittkey to ~/.ssh

- Get the zypp-ci-utils project:
# cd ~
# git config --global user.name 'zypp ci'
# git config --global user.email zypp-internal@suse.com
# git clone git@github.com:openSUSE/zypp-ci-utils.git


- Lauch an ssh-agent
Call ($ZCI_UTILS_CHECKOUT/zypp-team/bin/)ssh4cron to launch an ssh-agent
if not yet running and add the zypp-team-submittkey (passphrase needed). You
can call it anytime to make sure the key is available (e.g. after reboot).

(The launched agents env vars are stored in ~/.ssh4cron. Sourcing it gives you
access to the agent. That's done by bashrc if ~/.ssh4cron


- Copy and setups config files:
# mkdir --parents "$ZCI_USER_CONFIGDIR"
# cp "$ZCI_UTILS_CHECKOUT"/zypp-team/cfg/* "$ZCI_USER_CONFIGDIR"

Set auth tokens in oscrc and gitea-config so the configuration allows to
access IBS/OBS/GITEA as user zypp-team. Extending the PATH will then provide
git-ibs-zt  git-obs-zt  isc-zt  osc-zt commands to access IBS/OBS/GITEA as user
zypp-team. Scripts in "$ZCI_UTILS_CHECKOUT/zypp-team/bin" will refer to these
commands.


- Setup the ZCI_WORKSPACE:
# mkdir --parents "$ZCI_WORKSPACE"
# touch "$ZCI_WORKSPACE"/.giteastats

The magic .giteastats file is needed to enable using this directory for all
kinds of necessary checkouts.


##################################################
ZCI (ATM via docker):

See also zypp-ci-utils/docker.zci/README.
and zypp-ci-utils/zypp-team/bin/ZCI --help

Triggered by cron (crontab -l).

